# PX-42F remote control: a Samsung TV.
#
# Copy this file to the BIN/APPS/IR folder on the calculator's drive (USB
# Drive mode), then choose it in Settings > Games & Apps > Apps > IR. ON goes
# back to the menu.
# To make a remote for another device, copy this file, rename it, and change
# the codes. Lines starting with # are notes and are ignored.
#
# Each key is one entry:
#   name:     what the code does (shown at the top when it's sent)
#   label:    what the key shows on the screen (5 letters fit; 6 in the
#             rows from Up/7/8/9 down; 10 on ENTER)
#   button:   which key: R + row (0-6, from the top), C + column (0-5, from
#             the left)
#   protocol, address, command: the code, as in Flipper Zero .ir files
#             (Flipper-IRDB has codes for most TVs, players and amplifiers)
#
# The keys, and what this file puts on them:
#
#        C0       C1       C2       C3       C4       C5
#  R0    Sigma+   1/x      sqrt     LOG      LN       XEQ
#        Power    Input    Menu     Home     Guide    Info
#  R1    STO      RCL      Rdn      SIN      COS      TAN
#        Back     Left     Up       Down     Right    Exit
#  R2    ENTER    x<>y     +/-      E        <-       
#        OK       Mute     -        -        -
#  R3    Up       7        8        9        /
#        Ch+      7        8        9        -
#  R4    Down     4        5        6        x
#        Ch-      4        5        6        -
#  R5    SHIFT    1        2        3        -
#        -        1        2        3        Vol-
#  R6    ON       0        .        R/S      +
#        (Calc)   0        PreCh    -        Vol+
#
# A key with no entry stays blank and does nothing. R6C0 (ON) can't be used.
# SHIFT is left free: SHIFT and - held together save a screenshot.
#
name: Power
label: Power
button: R0C0
protocol: Samsung32
address: 07 00 00 00
command: 02 00 00 00
#
name: Source
label: Input
button: R0C1
protocol: Samsung32
address: 07 00 00 00
command: 01 00 00 00
#
name: Menu
label: Menu
button: R0C2
protocol: Samsung32
address: 07 00 00 00
command: 1A 00 00 00
#
name: Smart Hub
label: Home
button: R0C3
protocol: Samsung32
address: 07 00 00 00
command: 79 00 00 00
#
name: Guide
label: Guide
button: R0C4
protocol: Samsung32
address: 07 00 00 00
command: 4F 00 00 00
#
name: Info
label: Info
button: R0C5
protocol: Samsung32
address: 07 00 00 00
command: 1F 00 00 00
#
name: Return
label: Back
button: R1C0
protocol: Samsung32
address: 07 00 00 00
command: 58 00 00 00
